-- 必修一 U1 reading/cloze/listening 答案确定性打散(全A/偏斜→均匀)。id键 jsonb UPDATE,设固定值=幂等。Aaron 跑。
BEGIN;
-- 阅读 24题:A:24 B:0 C:0 D:0 → A:6 B:6 C:6 D:6
UPDATE public.junior_reading SET questions='[{"q":"According to the letter, what is Chen Lei''s problem?","answer":"D","options":["He never does his homework.","He has no friends at school.","He is often late for class.","He spends too much time playing computer games online."],"explanation":"信中说 your friend plays computer games too often and spends too much time online。"},{"q":"What is Susan Luo''s main piece of advice?","answer":"A","options":["Talk to the friend and encourage him to try new hobbies.","Report the friend to the teacher.","Stop being his friend.","Take away his computer."],"explanation":"她建议 talk to your friend about his behaviour 并 encourage him to try new hobbies。"},{"q":"According to the letter, why is spending too much time online a problem?","answer":"C","options":["It costs too much money.","It is against school rules.","It is unhealthy and makes it hard to focus on other things.","It makes people fluent in English."],"explanation":"原文:unhealthy, and it makes it very difficult to focus on other things in life。"},{"q":"Why does Susan Luo think the friend will listen?","answer":"D","options":["Because she is a teacher.","Because his parents asked him to.","Because he is afraid of her.","Because they are good friends."],"explanation":"原文:I am sure he will listen to you, since you are his good friend。"}]'::jsonb WHERE id='7e9f297e-d9a8-4451-a562-f0cf60668475';
UPDATE public.junior_reading SET questions='[{"q":"What do members of the Nature Club do?","answer":"A","options":["Grow plants and work in a greenhouse.","Learn new dance movements.","Help old people.","Debate different topics."],"explanation":"原文:In the Nature Club, they grow plants and work in a greenhouse。"},{"q":"According to the passage, who may do well in the Debate Club?","answer":"B","options":["A student who loves plants.","A student who speaks well.","A student who can dance.","A student who likes cleaning parks."],"explanation":"原文:A student who speaks well may do well in the Debate Club。"},{"q":"What is the FIRST thing you should think about when choosing a club?","answer":"A","options":["What you are interested in.","How much it costs.","Which club your friends joined.","How far the club is."],"explanation":"原文:First, think about what you are interested in。"},{"q":"What is the main idea of the passage?","answer":"C","options":["Why ballet is difficult to learn.","How to grow plants in a greenhouse.","How to choose a suitable school club.","Why debate is the best club."],"explanation":"全文介绍各社团并给出选社团的方法,主旨是如何选合适的社团。"}]'::jsonb WHERE id='81740cf9-fae2-4319-b2f5-f5db7dacdf65';
UPDATE public.junior_reading SET questions='[{"q":"Why did the writer feel anxious on the first morning?","answer":"B","options":["She forgot her textbooks.","She is not very outgoing and worried about making friends.","She was late for class.","She did not like the school."],"explanation":"原文:I''m not very outgoing ... Will I make any friends? What if no one talks to me?"},{"q":"How was the writer''s first maths class?","answer":"B","options":["Easy and boring.","Difficult, but the teacher was kind and friendly.","Cancelled because of the lab.","Too noisy to hear anything."],"explanation":"原文:My first maths class was difficult, but the teacher was kind and friendly。"},{"q":"Why couldn''t the writer concentrate in the chemistry class?","answer":"C","options":["The lab was too old.","She felt sick.","The guy next to her talked the whole time.","The teacher spoke too fast."],"explanation":"原文:the guy next to me talked the whole time, and I couldn''t concentrate on the experiment。"},{"q":"How did the writer feel by the evening?","answer":"D","options":["More anxious than before.","Angry with her classmates.","Sorry that she came to the school.","More confident than in the morning."],"explanation":"原文:I feel much more confident than I did this morning。"}]'::jsonb WHERE id='9c8af0d2-4ee1-4eca-afee-90e09322224d';
UPDATE public.junior_reading SET questions='[{"q":"Why was Adam''s first week of senior high school \"a little confusing\"?","answer":"B","options":["He could not find his classroom.","He had to make many new choices, such as courses and activities.","He did not know any of the teachers.","He was new to the city."],"explanation":"首段说他要仔细选课、选课外活动,新选择多,所以感到 confusing。"},{"q":"Why did the adviser recommend advanced literature to Adam?","answer":"A","options":["Because Adam likes English and is good at it.","Because it is an easy course.","Because Chinese is too difficult.","Because the football team needed him."],"explanation":"原文:because I like English and I''m good at it。"},{"q":"What does \"make the team\" in the passage mean?","answer":"D","options":["To set up a new team.","To beat the other team.","To train the team.","To be chosen as a member of the team."],"explanation":"make the team 指被选进球队;他说明年要 improve 才能进队。"},{"q":"What can we learn about Adam from the passage?","answer":"A","options":["He stays positive and does not give up easily.","He regrets coming to senior high school.","He dislikes all his courses.","He has given up sports for ever."],"explanation":"他没进球队但说 I won''t quit、I''ll find a way to improve,且 happy to be here,可见积极不放弃。"}]'::jsonb WHERE id='a5c833b2-470a-45d8-8386-a59c06706d2d';
UPDATE public.junior_reading SET questions='[{"q":"Why do senior high students often feel there is not enough time?","answer":"B","options":["They sleep too much.","They have more homework, subjects and activities.","They have no hobbies.","Their classes are too short."],"explanation":"原文:more homework, more subjects, and more extra-curricular activities than before。"},{"q":"According to the passage, what is a schedule?","answer":"A","options":["A plan that shows what you will do and when.","A list of your friends.","A kind of homework.","A school club."],"explanation":"原文:A schedule is a plan that shows what you will do and when。"},{"q":"Why should you leave some free time in your schedule?","answer":"D","options":["Because homework is not important.","Because teachers ask you to.","Because you have nothing to do.","Because all work and no play is not healthy."],"explanation":"原文:leave some free time ... because all work and no play is not healthy。"},{"q":"What does the writer think about good time management?","answer":"D","options":["It is impossible for teenagers.","It happens in only one day.","It is a waste of time.","It takes time but can become a useful habit."],"explanation":"原文:will not happen in one day, but if you keep trying, it will soon become a useful habit。"}]'::jsonb WHERE id='a5d9dff1-4552-4b18-8700-7cadb5a7ea73';
UPDATE public.junior_reading SET questions='[{"q":"What does the writer say teenagers are responsible for at school?","answer":"B","options":["Cleaning the whole school.","Their own studies and behaviour.","Teaching younger students.","Cooking for their classmates."],"explanation":"原文:At school, we are responsible for our own studies and behaviour。"},{"q":"What is the writer''s opinion about responsibility and freedom?","answer":"C","options":["They have nothing to do with each other.","Freedom is more important than responsibility.","They go together.","Responsibility means losing all freedom."],"explanation":"原文:responsibility and freedom go together。"},{"q":"According to the passage, what happens when you show you are responsible?","answer":"C","options":["You get less free time.","You have to do more homework.","Adults trust you more and give you more freedom.","Your friends stop believing you."],"explanation":"原文:adults trust you more and give you more freedom。"},{"q":"What does the writer think about making mistakes?","answer":"C","options":["They should never happen.","They mean you are not responsible.","They are a normal part of growing up.","They are always the parents'' fault."],"explanation":"原文:mistakes are a normal part of growing up。"}]'::jsonb WHERE id='aba25c32-72a6-415c-b843-ef1b1ecc4779';
